---
Run the supported SLM quality corpus in one warm Apple M4 CPU/NEON session

Usage: bitnet mac validate [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Configuration file path

      --model-id <MODEL_ID>
          Supported model id. Defaults to the validated Apple M4 SLM runtime artifact

          [default: qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-q8_0]

      --cache-dir <PATH>
          Override model cache root. Defaults to ~/.cache/bitnet-rs/models

  -d, --device <DEVICE>
          Device/backend label (cpu, cuda/gpu, hip/rocm, oneapi, npu/openvino-npu, nvidia-rtx-5070-ti-cuda/wgpu, intel-a770-opencl, metal/mpsgraph, apple-m4-metal, apple-m4-mpsgraph, apple-m4-cpu-neon, apple-m3-air-metal, apple-m3-air-mpsgraph, apple-m3-air-cpu-neon, auto). Apple M4 and M3 Air labels are distinct proof lanes

      --corpus <PATH>
          Deterministic SLM quality corpus

          [default: ci/quality/apple-m4-slm-quality-corpus.yaml]

      --log-level <LEVEL>
          Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)

      --corpus-repeat-runs <CORPUS_REPEAT_RUNS>
          Number of repeated runs for each corpus case

          [default: 2]

      --batch-size <SIZE>
          Batch size for processing

      --profile-set <PROFILE_SET>
          Validation profile set. Use accuracy for M3 comparison metadata, operator for 16/32/64 profiles, or performance for release-mode 16/32/64/128 profiles

          Possible values:
          - smoke:       Run the deterministic smoke corpus once
          - accuracy:    Run the deterministic quality corpus as an M3 accuracy comparison profile
          - operator:    Run bounded 16/32/64 warm-answer timing profiles and write an aggregate summary
          - performance: Run release-mode 16/32/64/128 warm-answer timing profiles

          [default: smoke]

      --max-new-tokens <MAX_NEW_TOKENS>
          Maximum new tokens per prompt when the corpus does not override it

          [default: 32]
          [aliases: --max-tokens, --n-predict]

      --threads <THREADS>
          Number of CPU threads to use (0 = all cores; deterministic mode may override)

          [default: 0]

      --allocation-audit
          Include scoped hot-loop allocation counter deltas in warm-session profile receipts

      --metal-prefill-qkv-phase
          Route the validated Q/K/V prefill Metal phase during the smoke quality corpus

      --progress
          Emit operator progress lines to stderr while validation runs

      --quiet
          Suppress validation status/progress lines; receipt artifacts are still written

      --json-out <PATH>
          Output aggregate warm-session receipt

          [default: target/apple-m4-productization/mac-validate.json]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
